!tags: Programming Regex

!id: nRoTOtgZ7v
!front: What does a regular expression pattern describe?
!back: A regex pattern describes a set of strings or substrings with a compact syntax. Matching asks whether the input contains a substring, or in full-match mode the whole input, that belongs to that set.
~~~

!id: glibidFmPK
!front: Compare a regex search with a regex full match.
!back:
- A search succeeds if some substring of the input matches the pattern.
- A full match succeeds only if the entire input matches the pattern.

Anchors or a full-match API are needed when the goal is validation rather than extraction.
~~~

!id: Fro2HnOzkH
!front: Compare consuming regex constructs with zero-width regex assertions.
!back:
- A consuming construct matches one or more input characters and advances the current position.
- A zero-width assertion checks a condition at the current position without consuming characters.
~~~

!id: BnjZrWGaZa
!front: Give three examples of zero-width regex constructs.
!back: Anchors, word boundaries, and lookaround assertions — each tests a condition at the current position without consuming any input characters.
~~~
